{
  "comment": "Ground effects left by moves on the arena grid (Terrain.cs). Everyone is affected (both teams), except the immuneTypes and, when grounded, the Pokémon that float or go through walls (movementType 2 and 3). sparesOwner (true when omitted): the Pokémon whose move left the terrain is not affected by it; false for ice and water, which act on their caster too. edge (round, blob, spiky, jagged, thorny) + edgeDepth (pixels): how the border of a patch is cut; flickerColor / flickerRate: the tile pulses between its colour and that one; speedMul: walking speed; boostTypes get boostMul instead; slideAccel: tiles/s² to change speed (ice: sliding), 0 = instant; knockbackMul: pushes last longer; status + statusChance (per second) + statusDuration (seconds, its own when 0); stun: seconds stunned every second spent there; fillColor: fills the holes of the tiles (no floor showing); damageShare: share of max HP lost per second; regenTypes heal regenShare of max HP per second; cures: status removed when standing there; navCost: extra path cost for the AIs (tiles of detour). moves: which move leaves which terrain (shape: trail along a shot, impact where it ends, around the user, dash along a melee dash, strike on a melee hit area); radius in tiles and duration in seconds come from the move's power through 'sizing' unless given; chance 0..1 (1 when omitted). reactions: a terrain painted (by) over another (on) gives 'becomes' instead ('' clears the cell, '=' keeps the old terrain); spread: the connected area of 'on' turns too, spreadDelay seconds per tile, at most spreadMax tiles away (0: all of it); duration: fixed seconds, else the old remaining time (keepDuration) or the new one, times durationMul.",
